DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI IngestXRayPage shipped at parity with the web source. A pure
@Observable orchestration model (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) owns the canonical
operator selection (vehicleId/window/bucket) and the two query lifecycles (web useVehicles +
useIngestXRay) over injectable seams (default = deterministic sample providers, the established
page+preview pattern), fanning each snapshot out to the four P3 surfaces (XRayControls,
XRayHeader, XRayBucketChart, XRayFieldsTable) through page-owned relays so the surfaces stay
vehicle-agnostic while the page coordinates them (the native analogue of the web parent-owns-
state composition). The page renders all four GlassPanels + the summary StatCard strip using
the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel/TSEmptyState/TSPageTitle/TSPanelTitle) — no
hand-rolled glass; every visible string from Localizable.xcstrings with web key names; gated
no-vehicle prompt vs. data surfaces; deep-linkable via the new .ingestXRay route (AppRouteParser
resolves /admin/ingest-xray) and hosted through the shell's route registry. Verified by the FULL
xcodebuild scheme GREEN (BUILD+TEST, 24447 tests / 0 failures, IngestXRayPageModelTests 15/15) on
the iPhone-16 (arm64) destination — the gate green required first repairing 5 pre-existing,
out-of-scope sibling defects, which were then reverted so the committed tree is in-scope only.

